1
00:00:03,253 --> 00:00:05,923
NOTHING! I CAN'T FIND ANYTHING
THAT I WANT TO EAT.

2
00:00:05,965 --> 00:00:07,591
EVERYTHING MAKES ME NAUSEOUS.

3
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:09,510
BEING PREGNANT
IS NO PIECE OF CAKE.

4
00:00:09,551 --> 00:00:10,552
OOH, CAKE.

5
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:12,596
NO.

6
00:00:12,638 --> 00:00:14,097
SEE?

7
00:00:14,139 --> 00:00:16,015
OH, HONEY, I'M SORRY.

8
00:00:16,057 --> 00:00:17,434
GOD... OOH!

9
00:00:17,476 --> 00:00:19,019
WHAT IS THAT SMELL?

10
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:21,897
IT'S COMING FROM
THE BATHROOM. OOH!

11
00:00:21,939 --> 00:00:25,150
WOW, PREGNANCY DOES GIVE YOU
SOME WEIRD CRAVINGS.

12
00:00:25,192 --> 00:00:26,234
( knocking )

13
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:27,235
Joey:
YEAH?

14
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:28,487
IT'S ME, PHOEBE.

15
00:00:28,529 --> 00:00:30,364
THERE'S SOMETHING
IN HERE I WANT TO EAT.

16
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:31,782
WHAT, WHAT...?

17
00:00:31,824 --> 00:00:33,951
WHAT SMELLS SO GOOD?

18
00:00:33,993 --> 00:00:35,786
IS IT THE SHAMPOO?

19
00:00:35,828 --> 00:00:36,954
IT'S GUAVA.

20
00:00:36,996 --> 00:00:38,079
NO!

21
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:39,164
EWW!

22
00:00:39,206 --> 00:00:40,541
OH, WAIT, WAIT!

23
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:43,585
IS IT MY
BOLOGNA
SANDWICH?

24
00:00:45,796 --> 00:00:47,088
YES. YES, YES, YES!

25
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:49,550
I CAN'T BELIEVE
THAT THE BABY WANTS BOLOGNA.

26
00:00:49,591 --> 00:00:51,468
THE BABY WANTS ME
TO EAT MEAT!

27
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:52,636
I CAN'T EAT MEAT!

28
00:00:52,678 --> 00:00:53,762
OH, WAIT, WAIT!

29
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:57,182
MAYBE IT'S THE PICKLE.

30
00:01:02,396 --> 00:01:07,568
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

31
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:09,820
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

32
00:01:09,862 --> 00:01:12,113
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

33
00:01:12,155 --> 00:01:17,118
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

34
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:19,538
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

35
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:22,666
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

36
00:01:22,708 --> 00:01:26,211
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

37
00:01:26,253 --> 00:01:28,589
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

38
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:31,258
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

39
00:01:31,299 --> 00:01:33,385
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

40
00:01:33,427 --> 00:01:36,179
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

41
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:41,184
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

42
00:01:48,734 --> 00:01:50,527
WHAT ARE YOU WRITING?

43
00:01:50,569 --> 00:01:52,362
WELL, JOSHUA'S
COMING IN TOMORROW

44
00:01:52,404 --> 00:01:54,907
AND SINCE I DON'T
HAVE THE GUTS
TO ASK HIM OUT

45
00:01:54,949 --> 00:01:56,450
I'M GOING
TO SELL HIM A COAT

46
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:58,201
AND PUT THIS NOTE
IN THE POCKET.

47
00:01:58,243 --> 00:01:59,369
OH, YEAH?

48
00:01:59,411 --> 00:02:02,372
"JOSHUA,
GIVE ME A CALL SOMETIME.

49
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:03,958
"GUYS LIKE YOU...

50
00:02:03,999 --> 00:02:06,835
NEVER GO OUT OF STYLE."

51
00:02:06,877 --> 00:02:09,046
WHAT DID YOU THROW AWAY?

52
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:11,172
Chandler:
HI, GUYS.

53
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:12,340
HI.

54
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:14,217
HEY, WHAT HAVE YOU GUYS
BEEN UP TO?

55
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:17,262
OH, WE WENT TO SEE
A COLLECTION OF
VICTORIAN DOORKNOBS

56
00:02:17,304 --> 00:02:18,889
AT THE COOPER
HEWITT MUSEUM.

57
00:02:18,931 --> 00:02:20,474
WITHOUT ME?!

58
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,184
YEAH. MY UNCLE
DRAGGED US THERE

59
00:02:23,226 --> 00:02:26,021
BUT IT ACTUALLY TURNED OUT
TO BE REALLY INTERESTING.

60
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:27,856
THEY WERE SO ORNATE
AND BEAUTIFUL.

61
00:02:27,898 --> 00:02:29,108
I MEAN, LOOK AT THAT.

62
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:31,068
I DON'T KNOW
HOW MUSEUMS WORK IN ENGLAND

63
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:32,527
BUT HERE, YOU'RE NOT SUPPOSED

64
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:33,737
TO TAKE STUFF.

65
00:02:33,779 --> 00:02:36,073
I, UH, I GOT IT
FROM THE GIFT SHOP.

66
00:02:36,115 --> 00:02:38,575
THEY HAVE REALLY
LAX SECURITY THERE.

67
00:02:39,785 --> 00:02:41,745
IT'S A JOKE.

68
00:02:43,497 --> 00:02:44,498
ALL RIGHT.

69
00:02:45,666 --> 00:02:47,250
RIGHT. I'VE GOT TO BE OFF.

70
00:02:47,292 --> 00:02:48,251
WELL, SEE YOU.

71
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:49,336
BYE-BYE, THEN.

72
00:02:49,377 --> 00:02:50,420
All:
BYE.

73
00:02:50,462 --> 00:02:51,922
WELL... HEY, YOU GUYS

74
00:02:51,964 --> 00:02:54,341
SEEM TO BE HAVING A GOOD TIME.

75
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:55,425
OH, YEAH.

76
00:02:55,467 --> 00:02:56,844
SHE'S-SHE'S AMAZING

77
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:59,178
AND-AND SHE'S SO MUCH FUN,
YOU KNOW?

78
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,722
AND YOU KNOW WHAT?

79
00:03:00,764 --> 00:03:02,683
WHEN I'M WITH HER, I'M FUN.

80
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:04,183
( laughs weakly )

81
00:03:04,225 --> 00:03:06,979
I EVEN SIGNED UP
FOR HELICOPTER CLASSES.

82
00:03:08,147 --> 00:03:10,357
SHE'S LEAVING IN TWO DAYS.

83
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:11,483
I DON'T HAVE
TO DO IT.

84
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:12,567
WOW. TWO DAYS.

85
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:13,777
YOU MUST BE BUMMED.

86
00:03:13,819 --> 00:03:15,570
SHE'S GOT TO GO BACK TO LONDON

87
00:03:15,612 --> 00:03:18,281
BUT I'VE BEEN PREPARED FOR THIS
FROM THE START.

88
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:20,408
WE BOTH KNEW
WE HAD TWO WEEKS TOGETHER

89
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:22,119
AND THEN THAT'S IT, YOU KNOW?

90
00:03:22,161 --> 00:03:25,497
HEY, THAT'S WHAT
ALL MY RELATIONSHIPS ARE LIKE.

91
00:03:25,539 --> 00:03:26,832
YES, BUT IN ROSS' CASE

92
00:03:26,874 --> 00:03:29,001
THEY BOTH KNOW
IN TWO WEEKS THAT'S IT.

93
00:03:30,878 --> 00:03:31,879
PHEEBS!

94
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,130
HEY!

95
00:03:33,172 --> 00:03:34,213
OH, HELLO! HELLO!

96
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:35,590
I KNOW, I
KNOW. YEAH.

97
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:40,137
SO, THE BABY
IS TOTALLY
CRAVING MEAT.

98
00:03:40,179 --> 00:03:42,139
THIS AFTERNOON,
I TRIED TRICKING IT.

99
00:03:42,181 --> 00:03:43,640
I MADE IT A SOY BURGER

100
00:03:43,682 --> 00:03:45,893
SO MAYBE IT WOULD THINK
IT WAS GETTING MEAT

101
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:47,227
AND I GOT NAUSEOUS.

102
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:50,564
WELL, MAYBE THAT'S BECAUSE
SOY BURGERS SUCK.

103
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:53,817
BEING PREGNANT
IS HARD ON YOUR TUMMY.

104
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:56,862
BUT AT LEAST YOU GET
THAT COOL, "PREGNANT LADY GLOW."

105
00:03:56,904 --> 00:03:58,072
OH, THAT'S SWEAT.

106
00:03:58,113 --> 00:03:59,073
YOU THROW UP ALL MORNING.

107
00:03:59,114 --> 00:04:00,824
YOU'LL HAVE
THAT GLOW, TOO.

108
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:09,708
OKAY.

109
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:12,086
OH, UH, HERE'S
THAT TRENCH COAT
THAT YOU WANTED.

110
00:04:12,127 --> 00:04:13,503
OH, GREAT, GREAT.

111
00:04:13,545 --> 00:04:14,796
WOW. YEAH.

112
00:04:14,838 --> 00:04:16,297
IT'S COMFORTABLE.

113
00:04:16,339 --> 00:04:17,674
YEAH.
MAN...

114
00:04:17,716 --> 00:04:20,343
I COULD REALLY FLASH SOMEBODY
IN THIS THING.

115
00:04:20,385 --> 00:04:22,012
OH, NO, NO. THEY
DON'T WANT YOU

116
00:04:22,054 --> 00:04:23,680
TO PUT YOUR HANDS
IN THE POCKETS

117
00:04:23,722 --> 00:04:25,390
UNTIL YOU ARE OUT OF THE STORE.

118
00:04:26,516 --> 00:04:27,517
WHY NOT?

119
00:04:27,559 --> 00:04:30,187
WELL, BECAUSE...

120
00:04:30,229 --> 00:04:33,232
WE GET A LOT OF...

121
00:04:33,272 --> 00:04:35,984
YOU KNOW,
THEY RUIN IT FOR EVERYBODY.

122
00:04:36,026 --> 00:04:37,611
I KNOW.

123
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:40,155
I WORE THAT CASHMERE SWEATER
ON A DATE LAST NIGHT.

124
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:42,032
OH.
YEAH.

125
00:04:42,074 --> 00:04:44,284
IT WAS THE FIRST DATE
SINCE THE DIVORCE.

126
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:46,536
WELL, CONGRATULATIONS.

127
00:04:46,578 --> 00:04:48,663
SO, DO YOU LOVE HER?

128
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:49,915
NO, NO, NO.

129
00:04:49,957 --> 00:04:52,167
SHE'S NICE,
BUT IT JUST MADE ME REALIZE

130
00:04:52,209 --> 00:04:55,045
I'M JUST NOT READY TO...
TO BE DATING, YOU KNOW?

131
00:04:55,087 --> 00:04:56,713
HUH.

132
00:04:56,755 --> 00:04:58,090
WELL...

133
00:04:58,132 --> 00:05:00,092
UH...

134
00:05:00,134 --> 00:05:01,093
THAT'S, UH...

135
00:05:01,135 --> 00:05:02,177
THAT'S INTERESTING.

136
00:05:02,219 --> 00:05:03,511
HEY, WHOA. HEY...

137
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:04,763
WHAT WAS THAT?

138
00:05:04,805 --> 00:05:07,015
OH, IT'S JUST AN
ANTI-THEFT DEVICE.

139
00:05:07,057 --> 00:05:09,392
THEN, UH, WH-WHAT'S THIS?

140
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:11,561
WELL, YOU NEED THAT,
YOU NEED THAT, TOO

141
00:05:11,603 --> 00:05:14,773
'CAUSE, OBVIOUSLY,
A THIEF COULD JUST
TEAR THIS RIGHT UP.

142
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:20,279
WE HAVE TO HAVE
A PARTY TONIGHT.

143
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,739
ACTUALLY, WE HAVE TO HAVE ONE
IN FIVE MINUTES

144
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:24,491
SO, EVERYBODY
CANCEL YOUR PLANS.

145
00:05:24,532 --> 00:05:26,285
WHAT ARE YOU
TALKING ABOUT?

146
00:05:26,325 --> 00:05:29,246
WE HAVE TO HAVE A SURPRISE
BON VOYAGE PARTY FOR EMILY

147
00:05:29,288 --> 00:05:30,956
BUT IT'S ACTUALLY FOR JOSHUA.

148
00:05:32,791 --> 00:05:35,335
LOOK. HE SAID
HE'S NOT READY TO DATE

149
00:05:35,376 --> 00:05:36,962
SO I HAD TO INVITE HIM
TO A PARTY

150
00:05:37,004 --> 00:05:38,922
IF I WANTED TO SEE HIM
OUTSIDE OF WORK

151
00:05:38,964 --> 00:05:40,339
AND NOW I HAVE CREATED

152
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:44,011
THE PERFECT OPPORTUNITY
TO SEDUCE HIM.

153
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:46,596
WELL, AS MUCH
AS I'D LIKE TO MEET JOSH

154
00:05:46,638 --> 00:05:47,722
AND WARN HIM...

155
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:51,392
EMILY AND I
AREN'T GOING TO BE HERE.

156
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:54,188
I MEAN, SHE'S GOING
TO COME BY FIRST TO SAY GOOD-BYE

157
00:05:54,229 --> 00:05:56,857
AND THEN I'VE GOT
A WHOLE SPECIAL EVENING PLANNED

158
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:57,983
SO, SORRY, NO PARTY.

159
00:05:58,025 --> 00:06:00,027
AW!

160
00:06:00,068 --> 00:06:01,320
HELLO.

161
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:03,571
SURPRISE!

162
00:06:04,823 --> 00:06:06,825
SURPRISE!
SURPRISE!

163
00:06:06,867 --> 00:06:11,121
NO ONE'S EVER THROWN ME
A SURPRISE PARTY BEFORE!

164
00:06:11,163 --> 00:06:13,707
WELL, IT WAS ALL ROSS' IDEA.

165
00:06:15,292 --> 00:06:18,419
YOU'RE SO SWEET...

166
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:20,339
AND I'M SO SURPRISED.

167
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:26,011
YOU REALLY DIDN'T KNOW?

168
00:06:36,188 --> 00:06:37,438
WHY ARE YOU OVER HERE

169
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,482
IF JOSHUA'S ALL
THE WAY OVER THERE?

170
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:42,027
UH, BECAUSE I'M TRYING
TO PLAY HARD-TO-GET.

171
00:06:42,069 --> 00:06:43,153
HE'S LOOKING.

172
00:06:43,195 --> 00:06:45,113
SAY SOMETHING FUNNY.

173
00:06:45,155 --> 00:06:46,573
LIKE WHAT?

174
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:48,825
( theatrical laugh )

175
00:06:48,867 --> 00:06:51,536
WH-WH-WHAT'S
SO FUNNY?

176
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:54,622
I SAID "LIKE WHAT?"

177
00:06:56,375 --> 00:06:59,336
WELL, THAT'S A THINKER.

178
00:06:59,378 --> 00:07:01,296
OKAY. THIS PLAYING
HARD-TO-GET THING

179
00:07:01,338 --> 00:07:02,339
IS NOT WORKING.

180
00:07:02,381 --> 00:07:04,341
HAND ME THOSE CHERRIES.

181
00:07:04,383 --> 00:07:05,926
OKAY.

182
00:07:05,967 --> 00:07:07,052
OKAY.

183
00:07:11,472 --> 00:07:12,515
HI.
HEY.

184
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:13,683
CARE FOR A CHERRY?

185
00:07:13,725 --> 00:07:15,352
OH, NO, THANKS.

186
00:07:15,394 --> 00:07:18,021
YOU KNOW, I CAN TIE
ONE OF THESE INTO A KNOT

187
00:07:18,063 --> 00:07:19,398
USING JUST MY TONGUE.

188
00:07:28,115 --> 00:07:29,908
( choking )

189
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:32,619
( coughing )

190
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,246
YOU OKAY?

191
00:07:34,288 --> 00:07:35,747
YOU ALL RIGHT?

192
00:07:41,044 --> 00:07:43,546
SO, WE SHOULD PROBABLY
GET GOING SOON.

193
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:46,341
OH, BUT THE PARTY'S
ONLY JUST GETTING STARTED.

194
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:48,718
WE HAVE TO BE
AT THE FOUR SEASONS FOR DRINKS

195
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:51,054
IN-- OH!-- 15 MINUTES,
AND THEN, UH, YOU KNOW

196
00:07:51,096 --> 00:07:52,555
THEN THE PLAZA FOR DINNER.

197
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:55,434
SO, WHY DID YOU PLAN A PARTY
AT THE SAME TIME?

198
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:58,312
NO, NO, NO. NO.

199
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:02,232
UM, ACTUALLY,
AMERICAN SURPRISE PARTIES

200
00:08:02,274 --> 00:08:03,984
ARE-ARE-ARE VERY SHORT.

201
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,693
IT'S USUALLY "SURPRISE!"

202
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:09,281
AND THEN, "OH, MY GOD,
I'M SO SURPRISED. GOOD-BYE."

203
00:08:10,991 --> 00:08:12,784
ROSS, I'M HAVING
SUCH A GREAT TIME.

204
00:08:12,826 --> 00:08:14,661
YOUR SISTER
HAS JUST BEEN
TELLING ME

205
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:17,205
THAT YOU USED TO DRESS
UP LIKE LITTLE OLD LADIES

206
00:08:17,247 --> 00:08:18,999
AND HOST MAKE-BELIEVE
TEA PARTIES.

207
00:08:22,836 --> 00:08:24,421
MONICA SAID THAT,
DID SHE?

208
00:08:24,463 --> 00:08:26,465
YEAH.

209
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:27,757
OH, YEAH.

210
00:08:27,799 --> 00:08:29,968
WHAT ARE YOU GOING
TO PUT ON TOP OF THAT?

211
00:08:30,010 --> 00:08:30,969
A LITTLE SALAMI.

212
00:08:31,011 --> 00:08:33,930
OOH, YEAH, YEAH.

213
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:37,058
THEN, UM, WHAT GOES
ON TOP OF THE SALAMI?

214
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:38,518
OH, PASTRAMI.

215
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:40,187
OOH, YEAH.

216
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:43,315
YOU'RE A GENIUS.

217
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:49,070
OH, COULD SOMEBODY
GIVE ME A HAND WITH THE ZIPPER?

218
00:08:51,281 --> 00:08:52,866
UP!

219
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:56,786
YOU CHANGED?

220
00:08:56,828 --> 00:08:59,456
YEAH. I DECIDED
I NEEDED MY LUCKY DRESS.

221
00:08:59,498 --> 00:09:01,624
AND "LUCKY" MEANS
MORE CLEAVAGE?

222
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:03,877
IT DOES FOR ME.

223
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:13,970
OH, GOD, LOOK AT HIM!

224
00:09:14,012 --> 00:09:15,138
HE'S SO CUTE!

225
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:16,723
I JUST WANT TO GO

226
00:09:16,764 --> 00:09:18,725
OVER THERE AND GRAB
HIM AND KISS HIM!

227
00:09:18,766 --> 00:09:20,018
HOW COULD I KISS HIM

228
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:22,187
WITHOUT LETTING HIM
KNOW THAT I LIKE HIM?!

229
00:09:22,229 --> 00:09:23,938
HEY, I KNOW
HOW YOU CAN GET HIM.

230
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:24,939
TAKE OFF YOUR BRA.

231
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:26,858
WHAT?

232
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,276
THIS SCENE
IN FOOTLOOSE...

233
00:09:28,318 --> 00:09:30,111
FLASHDANCE.

234
00:09:30,153 --> 00:09:31,946
YEAH. WITH THAT
PLUMBER GIRL...

235
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:32,906
SHE WAS A WELDER.

236
00:09:35,158 --> 00:09:37,244
WERE YOU, LIKE,
IN THE MOVIE, OR...?

237
00:09:39,454 --> 00:09:42,957
ANYWAY, SHE TAKES OFF HER BRA
UNDER THE SHIRT

238
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:45,210
AND PULLS IT OUT THE SLEEVE.

239
00:09:45,252 --> 00:09:47,045
VERY SEXY, AND CLASSY.

240
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:52,300
OR, IF YOU WANT
TO KISS HIM

241
00:09:52,342 --> 00:09:53,843
UM, YOU COULD
USE MISTLETOE.

242
00:09:53,885 --> 00:09:54,886
IT'S NOT CHRISTMAS.

243
00:09:54,928 --> 00:09:55,720
SPIN THE BOTTLE.

244
00:09:55,762 --> 00:09:56,930
HE'S NOT 11.

245
00:10:00,434 --> 00:10:01,851
THANK YOU SO
MUCH FOR THIS.

246
00:10:01,893 --> 00:10:03,770
IT WAS REALLY SO
THOUGHTFUL OF YOU.

247
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:05,230
WHAT, YOU'RE LEAVING?!

248
00:10:05,272 --> 00:10:06,773
WE HAVE
SOMETHING
TO GET TO.

249
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:09,192
YEAH. I THINK I'M
GOING TO TAKE OFF,
TOO, ACTUALLY.

250
00:10:09,234 --> 00:10:11,361
OH, YOU GUYS,
YOU CAN'T LEAVE YET!

251
00:10:11,403 --> 00:10:12,779
YOU HAVE TO STAY!

252
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:15,115
WE... WE'VE GOT
THE WHOLE BIG THING PLANNED.

253
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:16,824
WHAT BIG THING?

254
00:10:16,866 --> 00:10:19,119
SO, SPIN THE BOTTLE
WORKS LIKE THIS:

255
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,579
I SPIN THE BOTTLE...

256
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:23,748
LANDS ON GUNTHER,
SO I WOULD HAVE TO KISS GUNTHER.

257
00:10:25,792 --> 00:10:27,043
ALL RIGHT.

258
00:10:27,085 --> 00:10:29,588
WHO WANTS TO GO FIRST?

259
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,005
I'LL GO.

260
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:32,048
OKAY!

261
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:33,133
EMILY! WHOO!

262
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:37,678
WELCOME TO AMERICA.

263
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:43,477
ALL RIGHT.

264
00:10:44,894 --> 00:10:46,605
( Monica squealing )

265
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:48,273
TWO IN A ROW.

266
00:10:48,315 --> 00:10:50,484
YOU GOT TO USE
YOUR TONGUES NOW.

267
00:10:55,989 --> 00:10:57,574
ALL RIGHT.

268
00:10:58,450 --> 00:10:59,993
WHAT ARE THE ODDS?

269
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:01,202
WHAT ARE THE ODDS?

270
00:11:02,954 --> 00:11:06,082
OKAY. TH-THAT'S
ENOUGH, YOU KNOW?

271
00:11:06,124 --> 00:11:08,835
LET'S LET
SOMEONE
ELSE PLAY.

272
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:11,296
IF YOU DIDN'T WANT TO PLAY

273
00:11:11,338 --> 00:11:13,131
THEN WHY'D YOU COME
TO THE PARTY?

274
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:17,051
OKAY. MY TURN!

275
00:11:18,595 --> 00:11:19,678
OH!

276
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:21,722
LOOK AT THAT!

277
00:11:21,764 --> 00:11:23,141
OH, MY GOD!

278
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:28,729
OH, MY GOD, THE
BABY JUST KICKED!

279
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:29,897
OH!

280
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:31,065
IT'S OKAY, IT'S OKAY!

281
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:32,859
IF IT KICKED ONCE,
IT'LL KICK AGAIN!

282
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,235
( all clamoring )

283
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:37,947
ALL RIGHT.

284
00:11:37,989 --> 00:11:40,908
WELL, EVERYBODY JUST REMEMBER
WHERE THEY WERE SITTING.

285
00:11:49,626 --> 00:11:51,252
IT WAS A BUG.

286
00:11:55,465 --> 00:11:56,757
YOU KNOW WHY I'M NEVER

287
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:57,842
GOING TO EAT MEAT?

288
00:11:57,884 --> 00:11:59,010
'CAUSE IT'S MURDER.

289
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:00,428
IT'S COLD-BLOODED MURDER.

290
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:01,929
OKAY.

291
00:12:07,726 --> 00:12:09,688
THERE'S A PHOEBE
ON MY SANDWICH.

292
00:12:09,728 --> 00:12:11,690
MMM.

293
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:13,608
PHOEBE, WH-WHAT
ARE YOU DOING?

294
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:15,276
I CAN'T HELP IT.

295
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:17,445
I NEED THE MEAT.

296
00:12:17,487 --> 00:12:19,113
THE BABY NEEDS THE MEAT.

297
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:21,366
YOU KNOW HOW
WHEN YOU'RE DATING SOMEONE

298
00:12:21,408 --> 00:12:22,367
AND YOU DON'T WANT
TO CHEAT ON THEM

299
00:12:22,409 --> 00:12:24,369
UNLESS IT'S
WITH SOMEONE REALLY HOT?

300
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,498
YEAH. TOTALLY.

301
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:29,832
ALL RIGHT. OKAY.

302
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:31,876
WELL, THIS IS
THE SAME KIND OF DEAL.

303
00:12:31,918 --> 00:12:34,170
IF YOU'RE GOING TO DO
SOMETHING WRONG...

304
00:12:35,922 --> 00:12:37,465
DO IT RIGHT.

305
00:12:42,596 --> 00:12:45,098
SO YOU FEEL BETTER NOW?

306
00:12:45,139 --> 00:12:48,727
YEAH, BUT AT WHAT COST?

307
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:51,062
SIX MORE MONTHS,
THREE MEALS A DAY.

308
00:12:51,104 --> 00:12:53,231
I'M GOING TO EAT LIKE,
YOU KNOW...

309
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:55,233
MILLIONS OF COWS.

310
00:12:55,275 --> 00:12:59,320
HEY, WHAT IF I SAID I COULD
EVEN THINGS OUT FOR YOU...

311
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:00,655
MEAT-WISE?

312
00:13:00,697 --> 00:13:01,573
WHAT?

313
00:13:01,615 --> 00:13:03,491
I EAT A LOT OF MEAT, RIGHT?

314
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:05,910
BUT SUPPOSE, UNTIL
THE BABY'S BORN

315
00:13:05,952 --> 00:13:07,245
I LAID OFF IT.

316
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:09,080
NO EXTRA ANIMALS WOULD DIE.

317
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:11,082
YOU'D JUST BE
EATING MY ANIMALS.

318
00:13:11,124 --> 00:13:14,586
JOEY, I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU WOULD DO THAT FOR ME.

319
00:13:14,628 --> 00:13:16,087
ABSOLUTELY.

320
00:13:16,129 --> 00:13:18,298
I COULD BE A VEGETARIAN.

321
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:20,467
THERE'S NO MEAT IN BEER, RIGHT?

322
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:24,262
WE CAN STILL MAKE DINNER
IF WE SKIP APPETIZERS

323
00:13:24,304 --> 00:13:26,097
AND ASK FOR OUR CHECK
RIGHT AWAY.

324
00:13:29,517 --> 00:13:31,394
WELL, WE CAN'T
GO NOW.

325
00:13:31,436 --> 00:13:33,438
LOOKS LIKE
RACHEL'S GOING
TO PUT ON A SKIT.

326
00:13:35,607 --> 00:13:36,899
OH, MY GOD.

327
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:38,859
HAVE YOU LOST YOUR MIND?

328
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:40,570
NO. NO, NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

329
00:13:40,612 --> 00:13:42,322
I AM FINALLY
THINKING CLEARLY.

330
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:46,534
MY LUCKY DRESS WASN'T
WORKING OUT TOO WELL FOR ME

331
00:13:46,576 --> 00:13:49,828
BUT FOR FOUR YEARS,
THIS BABY NEVER MISSED.

332
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:52,332
RACHEL, RACHEL, RACHEL,
I CANNOT... I CAN'T LET...

333
00:13:52,373 --> 00:13:54,626
ACTUALLY, I KIND OF WANT
TO SEE WHAT HAPPENS.

334
00:13:57,629 --> 00:13:59,213
HEY.
HI.

335
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:01,257
NICE, UH... COSTUME.

336
00:14:01,299 --> 00:14:02,883
OH, YEAH.

337
00:14:02,925 --> 00:14:05,219
WELL, I WANTED TO GIVE EMILY

338
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:07,263
A BIG, AMERICAN
GOOD-BYE CHEER.

339
00:14:07,305 --> 00:14:08,931
SO, OKAY.

340
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:10,266
WHOO!

341
00:14:12,602 --> 00:14:13,561
READY?

342
00:14:13,603 --> 00:14:14,562
OKAY.

343
00:14:14,604 --> 00:14:16,105
GIVE ME AN "E."

344
00:14:16,147 --> 00:14:17,106
All:
"E"

345
00:14:17,148 --> 00:14:18,692
GIVE ME AN "M."
"M"

346
00:14:18,733 --> 00:14:20,276
GIVE ME AN "I."
"I"

347
00:14:20,318 --> 00:14:21,861
GIVE ME AN "L."
"L"

348
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:22,862
GIVE ME A "Y."

349
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:23,863
"Y"

350
00:14:23,904 --> 00:14:25,448
WHAT DO YOU GET?

351
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:27,742
EMILY.

352
00:14:27,784 --> 00:14:28,951
WHOO!

353
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:30,870
EMILY!

354
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:32,955
( yells )

355
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:35,458
OKAY, SO THAT'S ME
AS A CHEERLEADER.

356
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,459
TA-DUM!

357
00:14:36,501 --> 00:14:38,419
YOU ALL RIGHT?

358
00:14:38,461 --> 00:14:39,420
FINE. I'M FINE.

359
00:14:39,462 --> 00:14:40,755
I JUST LOOSENED A TOOTH.

360
00:14:40,797 --> 00:14:42,674
IT'S NO BIG DEAL.
I HAVE A DENTIST.

361
00:14:42,716 --> 00:14:44,175
I'LL GO PUT SOME ICE ON IT.

362
00:14:44,217 --> 00:14:45,218
EXCUSE ME.

363
00:14:46,927 --> 00:14:48,596
OKAY. WHAT DO I DO NOW?

364
00:14:48,638 --> 00:14:49,930
I THINK YOU'RE DONE.

365
00:14:51,558 --> 00:14:53,892
OKAY. TIME
TO TAKE OFF THE BRA.

366
00:14:56,563 --> 00:15:00,191
UH, THAT WAS...
REALLY, UH, GREAT

367
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:02,985
BUT I-I GOT TO
TAKE OFF, ACTUALLY.

368
00:15:03,027 --> 00:15:05,405
( whispers ):
TAKE THE BRA OFF.

369
00:15:08,324 --> 00:15:09,617
ALL RIGHT. COME ON.

370
00:15:09,659 --> 00:15:11,369
LET'S GO GET YOUR COAT.

371
00:15:11,411 --> 00:15:12,412
OKAY.

372
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:16,457
RACHEL IS MY GIRLFRIEND.

373
00:15:19,502 --> 00:15:22,046
SO THIS WAS,
UH, REALLY FUN.

374
00:15:22,088 --> 00:15:24,340
OH, YEAH. IT'S REAL FUN.

375
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:31,389
YOU KNOW, THIS BRA...

376
00:15:33,266 --> 00:15:37,228
IS REALLY BOTHERING ME.

377
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:39,522
YOU KNOW, THIS USED TO BE
MY BEDROOM.

378
00:15:39,564 --> 00:15:40,732
YEAH.

379
00:15:40,774 --> 00:15:43,192
LOT OF MEMORIES IN HERE.

380
00:15:43,234 --> 00:15:45,027
LOT OF MEMORIES.

381
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:48,322
IF THESE WALLS COULD TALK,
YOU KNOW WHAT THEY'D SAY?

382
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:50,825
WANT TO HEAR SOME MEMORIES?

383
00:15:56,581 --> 00:15:58,625
NEED A...
NEED A LITTLE HAND THERE?

384
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:00,877
OH, NO, NO.
I GOT THIS ALL UNDER CONTROL.

385
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:04,046
YOU REALLY DON'T
SEEM LIKE YOU DO.

386
00:16:04,088 --> 00:16:05,089
THAT'S...

387
00:16:08,259 --> 00:16:09,719
( grunts )

388
00:16:09,761 --> 00:16:11,220
( yells )

389
00:16:11,262 --> 00:16:12,764
FORGET IT!

390
00:16:12,806 --> 00:16:13,932
( groans loudly )

391
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:15,308
THIS IS... FOR...

392
00:16:16,643 --> 00:16:20,187
THIS IS NOT HOW THIS
WAS SUPPOSED TO HAPPEN.

393
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:21,815
WHAT WAS SUPPOSED TO HAPPEN?

394
00:16:23,316 --> 00:16:25,735
CAN YOU NOT LOOK AT ME
WHEN I SAY THIS?

395
00:16:29,656 --> 00:16:33,451
I THOUGHT THAT IF
I COULD GET YOU HERE

396
00:16:33,493 --> 00:16:35,995
I COULD SEDUCE YOU.

397
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:39,290
HUH.

398
00:16:39,332 --> 00:16:41,125
( groaning sigh )

399
00:16:41,167 --> 00:16:46,547
UH... I-I DON'T WEAR...
SUITS TO WORK

400
00:16:46,589 --> 00:16:49,091
AND I BOUGHT SIX OF THEM
FROM YOU.

401
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:51,010
WELL, I'M SORRY.

402
00:16:51,051 --> 00:16:53,012
I THOUGHT YOU NEEDED THEM.

403
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:54,889
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

404
00:16:54,931 --> 00:16:56,724
MY POINT IS
I KEPT COMING BACK

405
00:16:56,766 --> 00:16:58,643
BECAUSE...
I WANTED TO SEE YOU.

406
00:16:58,685 --> 00:17:00,144
WHY?

407
00:17:00,186 --> 00:17:01,980
BECAUSE I-I LIKE YOU.

408
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:04,649
YOU LIKE ME?

409
00:17:04,691 --> 00:17:06,317
YEAH.

410
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:10,404
I MEAN, YOU'RE-YOU'RE BEAUTIFUL
AND SMART AND SOPHISTICATED.

411
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:13,449
LOT OF THIS ISN'T, YOU KNOW,
BASED ON TONIGHT.

412
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:17,745
BUT-BUT YOU LIKE ME?

413
00:17:17,787 --> 00:17:19,580
OH, MY GOD,
I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

414
00:17:19,622 --> 00:17:23,334
ALL THIS TIME
I LIKED YOU AND YOU LIKED ME.

415
00:17:23,376 --> 00:17:24,627
BUT...

416
00:17:24,669 --> 00:17:26,295
NO, NO. DON'T SAY "BUT."

417
00:17:26,337 --> 00:17:28,006
NO, NO. BUT'S NEVER GOOD.

418
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:30,758
JUST LET'S LEAVE IT AT
I LIKE YOU AND YOU LIKE ME.

419
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:33,845
OKAY. UH, HOWEVER...

420
00:17:33,887 --> 00:17:36,931
NOW, SEE, THAT'S A FANCY "BUT."

421
00:17:36,973 --> 00:17:41,895
MY MARRIAGE, LIKE,
JUST ENDED

422
00:17:41,936 --> 00:17:46,941
AND I'M REALLY NOT READY
TO GET INTO ANYTHING YET.

423
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:49,903
BUT...

424
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,613
I'M SORRY.

425
00:17:52,655 --> 00:17:55,199
I... I JUST NEED
A LITTLE TIME.

426
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:00,329
OKAY.

427
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:05,501
OH, THERE YOU ARE.

428
00:18:05,543 --> 00:18:07,420
I WAS LOOKING
FOR YOU BEFORE.

429
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:10,673
JOSHUA'S GONE
SO YOU AND EMILY ARE FREE TO GO.

430
00:18:10,715 --> 00:18:12,008
IT'S OKAY.

431
00:18:12,050 --> 00:18:15,219
SHE'S STILL IN THERE
ENJOYING HER FAKE PARTY

432
00:18:15,261 --> 00:18:16,888
AND, UH, IT'S TOO LATE

433
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:19,891
TO DO ANY OF THE STUFF
I HAD PLANNED, SO...

434
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:22,810
OH, ROSS, I'M SORRY.

435
00:18:22,852 --> 00:18:24,729
I COMPLETELY RUINED
YOUR EVENING.

436
00:18:24,771 --> 00:18:25,730
( clears throat )

437
00:18:25,772 --> 00:18:26,731
YEAH.

438
00:18:26,773 --> 00:18:28,816
WELL, IF IT MAKES YOU

439
00:18:28,858 --> 00:18:32,361
FEEL ANY BETTER,
I MADE A FOOL OF MYSELF.

440
00:18:33,947 --> 00:18:35,155
HELPS A LITTLE.

441
00:18:36,616 --> 00:18:40,119
IS THERE ROOM ON THAT STEP
FOR A PATHETIC LOSER?

442
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,495
YEAH. HAVE A SEAT.

443
00:18:44,916 --> 00:18:46,626
OH...

444
00:18:48,586 --> 00:18:50,630
I'M SO SORRY.

445
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:52,048
IT'S OKAY.

446
00:18:52,090 --> 00:18:54,884
I MEAN, IT WAS JUST
A TWO-WEEK THING ANYWAY.

447
00:18:54,926 --> 00:18:57,804
I JUST DIDN'T WANT IT TO END
THIS WAY, YOU KNOW?

448
00:18:57,845 --> 00:19:01,057
OR MAYBE YOU DIDN'T
WANT IT TO END.

449
00:19:01,099 --> 00:19:02,892
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

450
00:19:02,934 --> 00:19:05,645
YOU SEEM TO REALLY LIKE HER.

451
00:19:07,772 --> 00:19:10,566
YEAH. I REALLY DO.

452
00:19:10,608 --> 00:19:12,568
YEAH, BUT WHAT AM I
GOING TO DO?

453
00:19:12,610 --> 00:19:13,903
I MEAN, WE BOTH AGREED

454
00:19:13,945 --> 00:19:15,905
IT WAS GOING TO BE
A TWO-WEEK THING.

455
00:19:15,947 --> 00:19:17,907
YOU KNOW, NO COMMITMENT.

456
00:19:19,784 --> 00:19:24,914
ROSS, THAT GIRL JUST SPENT
THE ENTIRE EVENING

457
00:19:24,956 --> 00:19:26,916
TALKING TO YOUR FRIENDS

458
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:29,085
ASKING TO HEAR
STORIES ABOUT YOU

459
00:19:29,127 --> 00:19:31,587
LOOKING THROUGH
MONICA'S PHOTO ALBUMS.

460
00:19:31,629 --> 00:19:33,589
I MEAN, YOU DON'T DO THAT

461
00:19:33,631 --> 00:19:35,800
IF YOU'RE JUST IN IT
FOR TWO WEEKS.

462
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:38,094
YOU THINK?

463
00:19:38,136 --> 00:19:40,513
LOOK, YOU'VE GOT,
LIKE, 14 HOURS

464
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:43,099
UNTIL SHE HAS TO
BE AT THE AIRPORT

465
00:19:43,141 --> 00:19:46,268
AND YOU'RE SITTING HERE
IN A HALLWAY WITH A...

466
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:49,981
28-YEAR-OLD CHEERLEADER
WITH A FAT LIP.

467
00:19:50,023 --> 00:19:51,357
( chuckles )

468
00:19:52,692 --> 00:19:53,985
YEAH. YOU'RE RIGHT.

469
00:19:54,027 --> 00:19:55,361
YEAH.

470
00:20:00,158 --> 00:20:01,367
THANKS.

471
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:08,499
WHAT PHOTO ALBUM WAS IT?

472
00:20:08,541 --> 00:20:09,834
I DON'T KNOW.

473
00:20:09,876 --> 00:20:12,045
IT WAS YOU
AND A BUNCH OF ALBINO KIDS.

474
00:20:15,006 --> 00:20:16,132
OH, MY GOD.

475
00:20:16,174 --> 00:20:17,758
THOSE WEREN'T ALBINO KIDS.

476
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:19,093
THAT WAS COMPUTER CAMP.

477
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:20,136
RACH.

478
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:24,849
HEY.

479
00:20:24,891 --> 00:20:25,850
HEY.

480
00:20:25,892 --> 00:20:27,643
YOU'RE A PATHETIC LOSER, RIGHT?

481
00:20:27,685 --> 00:20:29,687
( laughing ):
OH, YEAH.

482
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:30,938
SIT.

483
00:20:37,528 --> 00:20:38,571
HI.

484
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:40,322
OH, MY GOD.

485
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:41,824
JOSHUA.

486
00:20:41,866 --> 00:20:43,242
LOOK...

487
00:20:43,283 --> 00:20:47,371
ALL THOSE THINGS I SAID
ABOUT NOT BEING READY...

488
00:20:47,413 --> 00:20:48,414
THEY'RE NOT TRUE.

489
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:50,124
NO. THEY'RE-THEY'RE
ALL TRUE.

490
00:20:50,166 --> 00:20:52,292
OH.

491
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:53,961
BUT...

492
00:20:54,003 --> 00:20:56,254
OH.

493
00:20:56,296 --> 00:20:58,883
OH, I LOVE THAT "BUT."

494
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:11,353
UM, DO YOU WANT
TO GO INSIDE AND
GET SOME COFFEE?

495
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:12,354
YEAH.

496
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:13,397
OKAY.

497
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:22,406
EVERY TIME.

498
00:21:27,954 --> 00:21:28,996
WHAT DO YOU GOT?

499
00:21:29,038 --> 00:21:29,997
PASTRAMI.

500
00:21:30,039 --> 00:21:32,541
YEAH.

501
00:21:34,252 --> 00:21:35,628
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT
GOES GOOD WITH THAT?

502
00:21:35,669 --> 00:21:36,879
MM-HMM. CORNED BEEF.

503
00:21:36,921 --> 00:21:39,298
OOH, I WAS GOING
TO SAY BOLOGNA

504
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:40,883
BUT THAT'S MUCH BETTER.

505
00:21:40,925 --> 00:21:43,970
HEY, HOW ABOUT A LITTLE
OF THAT SMOKED TURKEY?

506
00:21:44,011 --> 00:21:45,471
OKAY.

507
00:21:45,512 --> 00:21:47,140
( laughing )

508
00:21:47,181 --> 00:21:49,809
OH, MAMA.

509
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:52,186
HOW... WHEN-WHEN
IS THE BABY DUE?

510
00:21:52,228 --> 00:21:53,062
SIX MONTHS.

511
00:21:53,104 --> 00:21:54,312
OH... HEY, NOW

512
00:21:54,354 --> 00:21:56,356
IF A COW SHOULD DIE
OF NATURAL CAUSES

513
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:58,109
I CAN HAVE ONE
OF THOSE, RIGHT?

514
00:21:58,151 --> 00:22:00,278
NOT IF I GET THERE FIRST.

515
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:02,863
